==English==

===Etymology===
From [[shebang]].

===Noun===
'''[[whole]] [[shebang]]'''

# {{idiom}} [[everything|Everything]]; the [[entire]] [[thing]].
#:''The festival had balloons, flowers, fireworks, performers, and the '''whole shebang'''.''
# {{idiom}} A [[building]] or [[house]] and everything in it.

